usage: orion_pro_rds.py [-h] [--plan | --preflight | --check-apply | --apply]
                        [--label LABEL] [--acceptance ACCEPTANCE]
                        [--acceptance-sha256 ACCEPTANCE_SHA256]
                        [--preflight-receipt PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT]
                        [--preflight-sha256 PREFLIGHT_SHA256]
                        [--expect-commit EXPECT_COMMIT]
                        [--expect-model-sha256 EXPECT_MODEL_SHA256]
                        [--expect-012-sha256 EXPECT_012_SHA256]
                        [--expect-013-sha256 EXPECT_013_SHA256]

Guarded existing-RDS schema/bootstrap pilot. Default is read-only preflight.
No DSN/credential arguments, cloud resources, source import, reset or
rollback. The explicit apply mode is separate from every default/offline/read-
only mode.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --plan                Offline plan only; no cloud or database access
  --preflight           Read-only AWS/SQL preflight (default)
  --check-apply         Offline apply-gate validation; never connects or
                        applies
  --apply               Explicit guarded schema/bootstrap transaction after
                        owner review
  --label LABEL
  --acceptance ACCEPTANCE
  --acceptance-sha256 ACCEPTANCE_SHA256
  --preflight-receipt PREFLIGHT_RECEIPT
  --preflight-sha256 PREFLIGHT_SHA256
  --expect-commit EXPECT_COMMIT
  --expect-model-sha256 EXPECT_MODEL_SHA256
  --expect-012-sha256 EXPECT_012_SHA256
  --expect-013-sha256 EXPECT_013_SHA256
